[font=Palatino Linotype][center][size=6][b][color=#6FCB9F]Bureau of Acceptable Views[/color][/b][/size]
[color=#8C8A82]Your camera, your rules.[/color][/center]



[color=#6FCB9F]Version: 3.11.012748[/color]

Camera-toggle reliability and manual-zoom preservation fixes.

- Fixed balanced camera-probe calls incorrectly disabling first-person view interception in mounted, werewolf, and swimming states.
- Fixed stale deferred camera toggles overwriting manual zoom and the remembered third-person distance; newer verified distance changes now cancel queued toggles and retries.
- Balanced camera-probe pairs now preserve the exact current distance, including close zoom below the remembered-distance threshold and native camera transitions.
- Kept protection against real rapid view oscillation, with one-shot observation cleaned up on zone changes and emergency camera reset.


[color=#6FCB9F]Version: 3.10.224232[/color]

This release is focused specifically on making PvP camera control direct, predictable, and player-owned.

- Replaced the Adaptive PvP situation-profile system with one lightweight PvP world mode.
- Removed scouting, mounted, pursuit, engaged, pressure, low-health, burst-damage, stability-lock, and outward-only zoom-assist mechanics.
- PvP mode no longer applies automatic distance, FOV, shoulder, or camera-offset changes and no longer uses ContextPresets, FovArbiter, Ease, or CameraResponse.
- Removed all PvP combat, health, sprint, damage, and safety observers; the mode now samples the world only on player activation or configuration changes.
- Kept the dedicated player-controlled PvP zoom step.
- Kept optional camera-shake suppression with a persisted snapshot so the player's original value survives and restores after `/reloadui` or an interrupted session.
- Simplified the settings panel to Enable PvP mode, PvP zoom step, and Allow camera shake in PvP.
- Added a separate testing and feedback notice inviting players to share experience-based requests on the addon forum.


[color=#6FCB9F]Version: 3.9.000146[/color]

Unified camera response, input reliability, and dependency clarity update.

- Added one global Camera response profile shared by Dynamic FOV, context presets, Adaptive PvP framing, and over-the-shoulder movement.
- Added As in ESO, Instant, Responsive and Smooth response modes.
- Added coordinated temporary suspension of ESO camera smoothing so overlapping BAV transitions cannot restore it early; emergency and load-screen recovery remain immediate.
- Migrated existing smoothing preferences automatically and replaced the two separate smoothing checkboxes with one response dropdown.
- Fixed live offset smoothing suspension, rejected fast writes, and false restore-success notices.
- Adaptive PvP now recognizes native mouse-wheel and gamepad zoom as manual distance control.
- Clarified that LibAddonMenu-2.0 is a required dependency.


[color=#6FCB9F]Version: 3.8.145105[/color]

Live camera-offset keybinds with a remembered home pose.

- Added hold-to-nudge keybinds for third-person horizontal offset (left/right) and vertical offset (up/down). Movement is continuous and speed-scaled (50-200% in settings).
- Offset binds stay locked until one home pose is captured from the Live offset nudge settings tab.
- Restore returns horizontal and vertical offsets to that remembered pose; nudging never overwrites home. Zoom, field of view, and shoulder are unchanged.
- Added Remember, Restore, and Delete buttons, plus a centred on-screen notice for live offsets and for blocked, remembered, restored, and deleted states.
- Context-preset restore snapshots follow live offset nudges, so leaving a state does not rewind the framing you just set.


[color=#6FCB9F]Version: 3.7.105247[/color]

Update 51 compatibility and sprint-state reliability update.

- Audited the addon against the future Update 51 / API 101051 documentation and API patch notes; no incompatible removed or changed API usage was found.
- Added API 101051 manifest compatibility while retaining support for the current live API 101050.
- Replaced the legacy werewolf compatibility alias with the documented `IsPlayerInWerewolfForm()` API.
- Removed the sprint detector's dependency on undocumented roll-dodge action results.
- Added a bounded roll-dodge suppression window so sprint detection always recovers when ESO omits a matching completion event.


[color=#6FCB9F]Version: 3.6.064722[/color]

Patch release with Adaptive PvP fixes, stability improvements, and runtime optimizations.


[color=#6FCB9F]Version: 3.5.155700[/color]

Added a clear notice that Adaptive PvP is currently in testing and will continue to be improved and fixed based on test results.


[color=#6FCB9F]Version: 3.4.210432[/color]

Quick patch with small PvP camera refinements: outward-only zoom assistance that yields to manual input, camera shake disabled by default, and a slightly more responsive zoom step.


[color=#6FCB9F]Version: 3.4.200215[/color]

A major feature release focused on reliable, situation-aware PvP camera framing.

- Added Adaptive PvP mode, enabled by default and active only in AvA worlds and Battlegrounds.
- Added stable scouting, mounted scouting, pursuit, engaged, pressure, and suspended states with explicit priority.
- Added rolling burst-damage and low-health pressure detection, gank entry, and a critical-health framing lock.
- Added automatic suspension for death, siege camera control, partial profile writes, and sustained camera-distance write rejection.
- Added minimum state holds and timed pressure/gank release so rapid combat events cannot oscillate zoom or FOV.
- Added configurable PvP feature toggles and health/burst thresholds to the English and Russian settings panels.
- Routed every PvP profile through ContextPresets snapshot/restore and FovArbiter ownership; PvPMode never rotates the camera or writes camera settings directly.
- Limited combat, health, sprint, and safety observers to active PvP worlds and rebuilt state from fresh samples after every zone activation.
- Fixed external profiles not applying when ordinary Context Presets were disabled.
- Fixed PvP framing surviving a transition back into PvE or being reasserted from stale world state.
- Normalized related low-health and critical-health settings so saved values cannot drift from runtime values.
- `/bav reset` now suspends Adaptive PvP for the remainder of the current PvP world before restoring the player's camera.
- Fixed the emergency camera reset immediately re-applying a Manual or sprint-triggered over-the-shoulder position.

[b][color=#6FCB9F]Adaptive PvP mode[/color][/b]

Adaptive PvP does not react to every hit with another camera movement. It reduces combat, sprint, mount, health, recent damage, death, siege ownership, and camera-write health into one stable state, then applies at most one conservative profile. Threat escalation is immediate; exits are held long enough to prevent jitter. At critical health the established combat frame is kept stable, and any unsafe engine ownership or failed apply suspends the module instead of retrying through the fight. Outside PvP, its heavy observers are unregistered and the player's own framing is restored.


[color=#6FCB9F]Version: 3.3.163944[/color]

An update focused on optimizing existing features and fixing a bunch of bugs.

- Fixed an active Context Preset being saved as the player's normal zoom during logout, zone changes, or `/reloadui`.
- Fixed stale FPV reconciliation intent sometimes preventing the camera from returning to third person.
- Preset and shoulder recovery snapshots are now retained until every restore write succeeds.
- Over-the-shoulder framing no longer applies unless the player's original shoulder position was captured successfully.
- FOV holds now report failed engine writes correctly and release newly-acquired ownership on failure.
- Dynamic FOV now snapshots and persists the player's manual FOV, restoring it when the feature is disabled or after interrupted sessions.
- Added a lightweight distance observer so Dynamic FOV follows controller and native game camera zoom changes.
- Camera inputs now pass through to ESO when the live zoom cannot be read, instead of writing from a fallback distance or corrupting SavedVariables.
- Reduced SprintWatch false positives with mounted, werewolf, swimming, siege, and roll-dodge guards plus two-sample sprint confirmation.
- Updated README performance details, removed obsolete self-check documentation, and repaired the module table.



[color=#6FCB9F]Version: 3.2.072916[/color]

- Fixed module debug and error logging never reaching the chat window (the LogDebug/LogError exports were missing).
- Fixed Context Presets committing a state whose bundle did not resolve, which left a phantom state and a bogus restore.
- The debug level now persists across sessions and ships silent by default.
- `/bav status` now reports accumulated camera-write failures instead of counting them silently.
- Fixed switching the over-the-shoulder mode while a preset is active leaving the shoulder offset baked in: an ownership change now hands the property back and re-bases the preset snapshot.
- Raised the zoom-write retry give-up message from debug to warning.
- Removed dead code: the duplicated sprint probe, the redundant FOV glide duration local, and unused localization strings.



[color=#6FCB9F]Version: 3.1.215837[/color]

- Removed the LibSprint dependency and moved its action-slot sprint heuristic into BAV's lazy event-driven SprintWatch.
- Removed Velocity FOV, its speed sampling, settings, debug overlay, and FOV boost integration.
- Removed obsolete SavedVariables migrations, `/bav dump`, diagnostic APIs, and related settings and localization.


[color=#6FCB9F]Version: 3.0.094246[/color]

- Fixed Dynamic FOV smoothing conflicting with context-preset FOV.
- Fixed preserving the original camera when a smooth preset exit is interrupted.
- Preset and OTS changes in LAM now apply immediately.
- Context Presets no longer overwrite shoulder while OTS owns it.
- Current player states are initialized when enabling presets and Auto OTS.
- Resetting Dynamic FOV immediately restores near/far FOV to engine defaults.
- Fixed preset recovery after `/reloadui`, login, and unexpected session termination.
- Velocity FOV now starts correctly with default settings.
- Features enabled from an already-open LAM panel now suspend camera writes correctly.
- OTS establishes shoulder ownership before Context Presets during startup.
- Removed the self-check module, its button, command, and related documentation.
- Removed conflict advisories and their settings toggle; the silent FPV safety backoff remains.
